        "original_id": "ae9c6421-daa9-55c5-a801-74737e142247",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Morning glory\n- Systems: Convolvulaceae taxonomy and systematics\n- Products: Sorbus\n- Systems: Rosaceae\n- Products: Albugo ipomoeae-panduratae\n- Topics: Ipomoea species\n\nFacts:\n- Morning glory is the common name for more than 1,000 species of flowering plants in the family Convolvulaceae.\n- Convolvulaceae taxonomy and systematics are currently in flux for the plants called morning glory.\n- Sorbus is a genus of about 100 to 200 species of trees and shrubs in the rose family Rosaceae.\n- Albugo ipomoeae-panduratae causes leaf and stem lesions on various Ipomoea species, including cultivated morning glories and related plants.",
